OpenVPN 2.7.9 with transport obfuscation patches
================================================

This is a modified build of OpenVPN 2.7.9. It is not an official OpenVPN
release and is not produced or endorsed by OpenVPN Inc.

Upstream source:  https://github.com/OpenVPN/openvpn
Upstream tag:     v2.7.9
Upstream commit:  7b60c2aa34992639691e3a2d651fe27301e2e9d5

Patches applied
---------------

The transport obfuscation patches come from:

    https://github.com/aw3r1se/ovpn-obfuscate-patches

Applied, in this order:

    general/0001-transport-core.patch
    udp/0001-enable-udp.patch
    tcp/0001-enable-tcp.patch
    wss/0001-enable-wss.patch

Each patch adds source files and build-system detection only. The patched
tree adds these directives:

    --obfuscate KEY                 TCP Scrambler
    --obfuscate-udp KEY PADDING     UDP obfuscation
    --wss-proxy HOST URI            WebSocket-over-TLS transport
    --wss-proxy-sni [NAME]
    --wss-proxy-header NAME [VALUE]
    --wss-proxy-allow-self-signed-cert

Obfuscation requires `--disable-dco`: the transport code runs in userspace,
above the socket layer, so kernel data-channel offload bypasses it. The client
also disables DCO on its own whenever an obfuscation transport is configured.

What changed relative to upstream
---------------------------------

Only the four patches listed above. No upstream source file is modified for
any other purpose. To reproduce this tree:

    git clone https://github.com/OpenVPN/openvpn.git
    cd openvpn
    git checkout --detach v2.7.9
    git apply <repo>/general/0001-transport-core.patch
    git apply <repo>/udp/0001-enable-udp.patch
    git apply <repo>/tcp/0001-enable-tcp.patch
    git apply <repo>/wss/0001-enable-wss.patch

Build (Windows x64)
-------------------

Requires Git, Python 3, CMake 3.21+, vcpkg, and a Visual Studio C++ toolset
with Spectre-mitigated libraries and a Windows SDK. Run from an x64 Native
Tools Command Prompt so `mc.exe` is on PATH.

    set VCPKG_ROOT=C:\path\to\vcpkg
    cmake --preset win-amd64-release -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=%VCPKG_ROOT%\scripts\buildsystems\vcpkg.cmake -DBUILD_TESTING=ON
    cmake --build --preset win-amd64-release --parallel
    ctest --test-dir out\build\win-amd64-release -C Release -R "^test_obfs_" --output-on-failure

Tested with Visual Studio 2022 (MSBuild 17.14) and OpenSSL 3.6.2.

Release contents
----------------

The Windows x64 archive contains the client, the service wrapper and the adapter
tool, all built from this tree:

    openvpn.exe             client and server
    tapctl.exe              create/list/delete VPN adapters
    openvpnserv.exe         Windows service wrapper
    openvpnservmsg.dll      event-log message table for the service
    openvpnmsica.dll        MSI custom actions, used only by installer builds
    libcrypto-3-x64.dll
    libssl-3-x64.dll
    libpkcs11-helper-1.dll
    legacy.dll              OpenSSL legacy provider, only needed for BF-CBC
    vcruntime140.dll        omit if the VC++ 2015-2022 Redistributable is installed
    COPYING
    LICENSE
    README.txt

Nothing is required beyond this archive for a client connection, for running
OpenVPN as a service, or for managing adapters from scripts.

`legacy.dll` is only needed when the server uses BF-CBC. `openvpnmsica.dll` is
only loaded by MSI-based installers; the other files are unused otherwise.

LZO and LZ4 are linked statically; no extra DLLs are required for compression.

